{"is_error":false,"duration_api_ms":143149,"num_turns":1,"stop_reason":"end_turn","session_id":"b5248b87-6243-4b77-99a4-6a05b3e4f4c4","total_cost_usd":0.77061,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42444,"cache_read_input_tokens":20672,"output_tokens":12277,"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42444,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":12277,"cache_read_input_tokens":20672,"cache_creation_input_tokens":42444,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":42444},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":28809,"outputTokens":18,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.028899,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty"},"claude-opus-5":{"inputTokens":2,"outputTokens":12277,"cacheReadInputTokens":20672,"cacheCreationInputTokens":42444,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.741711,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"canonicalModel":"claude-opus-5","provider":"firstParty"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\n  \"agent\": \"debris-designer\",\n  \"size_classes\": {\n    \"small\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 1,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 2,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true\n    },\n    \"medium\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 2,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 4,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": true\n    },\n    \"oversized\": {\n      \"slots_crushed\": 6,\n      \"slots_uncrushed\": 12,\n      \"hand_tetherable\": false\n    }\n  },\n  \"debris\": [\n    {\n      \"id\": \"scorched_hull_panel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Scorched Hull Panel\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 140,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 20,\n      \"notes\": \"Curved skin plate off something that already burned once — the commonest thing in the low sky and the piece every player learns to latch on first.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"bent_truss_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Bent Truss Section\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 380,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 14,\n      \"notes\": \"A folded aluminium lattice that crushes down well; two slots of honest tonnage and the first piece that makes the jetpack feel heavy.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"spent_booster_ring\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Spent Booster Ring\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 460,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"Interstage collar from a launcher that never made orbit — the heaviest hand-tetherable piece in the band, and a deliberate test of whether the player tows gently.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"insulation_blanket_wad\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Insulation Blanket Wad\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 60,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 18,\n      \"notes\": \"A balled-up wad of multi-layer foil: almost free to tow, but it still costs a full crushed slot, so it is the piece that teaches slot cost and mass are different currencies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"fairing_shard\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Fairing Shard\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 110,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 16,\n      \"notes\": \"A composite wedge off a shattered payload fairing — light, plentiful, and the reliable filler that keeps a lazy run breaking even.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_camera_dome\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Camera Dome\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 95,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"Star-cracked optical dome that still glints on a slow cycle; the player's first fragile piece, cheap enough to lose and instructive enough to matter.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"battered_antenna_whip\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Battered Antenna Whip\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 70,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A bent whip antenna on its feed block — the lightest fragile piece in the game, so a suborbital player can practise a gentle landing without much at stake.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"derelict_upper_stage\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Derelict Upper Stage\",\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1150,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"A whole dead kick stage tumbling slowly; crane-cable only and therefore out of reach in the shipping slice, present so the oversized class exists in the lowest band the player ever flies.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"satellite_bus_frame\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Satellite Bus Frame\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 500,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 14,\n      \"notes\": \"The structural box a satellite was built around, stripped of everything soft — the low band's bread-and-butter haul and the first piece that visibly slows the ride home.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cracked_solar_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cracked Solar Array\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 380,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 5,\n      \"notes\": \"A folded array wing with half its cells starred; never crushable, so it pays four uncrushed slots forever, and it is the archetypal fragile decision of the shipping slice.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"reaction_wheel_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Reaction Wheel Housing\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 300,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 16,\n      \"notes\": \"A dense steel flywheel can — one slot of concentrated mass, which is what makes the low band heavier per slot than suborbital without filling the hold faster.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"propellant_tank_shell\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Propellant Tank Shell\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 450,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"A punctured titanium sphere that crushes flat with a satisfying report; bulky before the compactor touches it, ordinary after.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gyro_package\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Gyro Package\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 260,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 13,\n      \"notes\": \"A sealed inertial unit, solid and unglamorous — the piece a cautious player fills the last slot with when the shield plate is already low.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"parabolic_dish_section\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Parabolic Dish Section\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 240,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A quarter-segment of a comms dish, thin-skinned and awkward on the line; it spawns off the clumps and high in the band, so reaching it is a real burn — and at two uncrushed slots it is a fragile detour a nearly full hold can still say yes to.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"star_tracker_head\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Star Tracker Head\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 210,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A shaded optical head the size of a coffee can — the rarest thing in the low band and the cheapest fragile piece to tow, which makes the detour tempting rather than obvious.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"tumbling_comsat_core\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Tumbling Comsat Core\",\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 2000,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"An intact comsat body spinning end over end; crane-cable only, deferred with the crane magnet, and the rehearsal object for the capstone capture.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"dense_avionics_core\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Dense Avionics Core\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1000,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 12,\n      \"notes\": \"A potted flight-computer block, solid metal and boards all the way through — the high band's workhorse and, at half a tonne per slot, the reason a full hold up here needs extra passes.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"shattered_solar_wing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Shattered Solar Wing\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 820,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 6,\n      \"notes\": \"A long array wing snapped mid-span, still glinting; the most frequently met fragile piece in the game and the one most often lost to a hot entry.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"iridium_battery_stack\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Iridium Battery Stack\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 1150,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 10,\n      \"notes\": \"A strapped column of cells wrapped in shielding — the heaviest hand-tetherable piece authored, and the clearest single expression of 'the valuable stuff fights you'.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"platinum_thruster_cluster\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Platinum Thruster Cluster\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 540,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 11,\n      \"notes\": \"Four scorched attitude nozzles on a common manifold, crammed with precious metal; one crushed slot, and the densest thing per slot a hand magnet can hold.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"optical_telescope_barrel\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Optical Telescope Barrel\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 900,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 4,\n      \"notes\": \"A baffled tube with the primary mirror still seated — heavy, fragile, uncrushable, and the piece that makes a player choose between a soft landing and one more pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"cryo_instrument_housing\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Cryo Instrument Housing\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"small\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 430,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 3,\n      \"notes\": \"A frosted dewar off a science payload, thin-walled and unforgiving; small enough to slip into a nearly full hold, fragile enough to be the first thing a hard touchdown wrecks.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"gold_foil_bus_module\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Gold Foil Bus Module\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"medium\",\n      \"fragile\": false,\n      \"mass_kg\": 980,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 9,\n      \"notes\": \"A foil-wrapped equipment bay torn cleanly off its bus — crushable, solid, and the safe high-band haul when the shield plate will not stand another hot pass.\"\n    },\n    {\n      \"id\": \"mirrored_survey_array\",\n      \"display_name\": \"Mirrored Survey Array\",\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"size_class\": \"oversized\",\n      \"fragile\": true,\n      \"mass_kg\": 2900,\n      \"spawn_weight\": 1,\n      \"notes\": \"A segmented mirror panel the size of a barn door: fragile and oversized at once, crane-cable only, deferred with the high band — it exists to preview the exact class Mr. Armstrong's satellite belongs to.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"band_summary\": [\n    {\n      \"band\": \"suborbital\",\n      \"piece_count\": 8,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.103,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 308.125\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"low\",\n      \"piece_count\": 8,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.179,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 542.5\n    },\n    {\n      \"band\": \"high\",\n      \"piece_count\": 8,\n      \"fragile_fraction\": 0.25,\n      \"mean_mass_kg\": 1090\n    }\n  ],\n  \"revision_notes\": [\n    \"Finding 1 (low-band medium mass) accepted, and it was the real one. Every low-band medium came down: satellite_bus_frame 700 -> 500, propellant_tank_shell 620 -> 450, cracked_solar_array 520 -> 380, parabolic_dish_section 480 -> 240 (see finding 3). The worst two-tether load a low-band player can build is now bus frame + tank shell = 950 kg instead of 1400 kg, so the Balancer's 0.35 m/s^2 case improves by about 45% at unchanged jetpack_thrust_n, and the empty astronaut is untouched. I did not go further, and the reason is a floor rather than a preference: suborbital's mediums are 380 and 460 kg, so any low-band medium below ~470 makes the low band lighter on the tether than the band beneath it and inverts the curve the whole catalog exists to hold. If playtesting still reads 950 kg as unresponsive, the residual is not a low-band problem — it is the hand-tether mass ladder as a whole, and the fix is to scale every non-oversized mass in this catalog by one factor so the band ordering survives, not to shave the low band again.\",\n    \"Finding 3 (fragile mediums eat 4 of 6 base slots) accepted in part, with one piece changed rather than two. parabolic_dish_section is now size_class small, 240 kg: at 2 uncrushed slots it is a fragile detour a player can say yes to with a third of the hold already full, which is the 'sometimes worth it' the GDD asks for. cracked_solar_array stays a fragile medium at 4 uncrushed slots on purpose — it is named in the GDD as the archetypal fragile decision, and if no fragile piece in the shipping slice ever costs two thirds of the hold then the fragile flag has no teeth in the band where the player learns it. So the low band now offers the fragile choice at both scales: two cheap ones (star tracker 1 slot crushed-equivalent cost of 2 uncrushed, dish section 2 uncrushed) and one expensive one. Slot costs themselves are untouched; they are the GDD's, not mine.\",\n    \"Finding 2 (iridium_battery_stack at 1150 kg sets the latch-shear ceiling) acknowledged and declined, with the mass left as authored. The Balancer's arithmetic is right and its conclusion is the design working: a 1.6 m/s gentle-latch requirement is a base-tier number quoted against a high-band piece, and no base-tier astronaut is ever in the high band. By the time the stack is reachable the player is on hand-magnet tier 3, which is exactly the upgrade the GDD says is bought to reach it. GDD 2.3.4 also states the failure is telegraphed half a second ahead and recoverable at low relative velocity, so the cost of getting it wrong is fuel and seconds, not the salvage. Trimming it by the 10-15% that would not disturb the band ordering would move the shear threshold by a fraction of a metre per second and buy nothing; trimming it enough to matter would delete the piece's entire reason to exist. It stays the ceiling deliberately, and it is the right number for hand_magnet tier 3 to be tuned against.\",\n    \"No ids were added, removed or renamed, and nothing outside the four low-band pieces above was touched. Both band_summary rows that could move were recomputed from the final piece list rather than carried forward: low mean_mass_kg is 4340/8 = 542.5, and its fragile_fraction is unchanged at (5+4+3)/67 = 0.179 because the reclassification moved a size class, not a spawn weight.\"\n  ],\n  \"design_notes\": [\n    \"Mass rises about 3.5x from suborbital to high on the plain per-piece mean (308.1 -> 542.5 -> 1090.0 kg), and about 4.4x if the crane-only oversized pieces are excluded (187.9 -> 334.3 -> 831.4 kg). That is the GDD 2.3.7 bet stated in numbers: the better the haul, the worse the ride home. The low-band revision flattened the sub-to-low step and steepened the low-to-high one, which is the honest consequence of making the shipping slice flyable — the slice the player actually meets this semester now climbs more gently, and the deferred band is where the curve gets its teeth back.\",\n    \"The figure that actually reaches the physics is mass per crushed slot, because slots are what cap a hold. Suborbital runs ~103 kg/slot on crushable smalls and ~210 on mediums; low runs ~280 and ~238; high runs ~540 and ~521. A 6-slot starting hold therefore weighs roughly 0.6-1.3 t from suborbital, 1.4-1.7 t from low, and ~3.2 t from high. Against the Researcher's 1400 kg staged ship that is beta 267 empty rising to ~460 from suborbital, ~560 from low and ~880 from the high band, i.e. two to three times the passes an empty ship needs. The catalog carries the band-to-band difficulty differential the Researcher warned entry speed alone could not (his note: only 1.35x flux from suborbital to high), which is exactly the beta lever he pointed at.\",\n    \"Note that the low band is now denser per slot on smalls (280 kg/slot) than on mediums (238 kg/slot). That inversion is deliberate and it is the band's identity: the reaction wheel housing and the gyro package are the pieces that make a low-band hold heavy, and they do it one slot at a time without filling the hold. It also means the low band's hold-limited weight barely moved in this revision even though its tether-limited weight dropped a third — the ride home is as heavy as it was; only the trip back to the hold got lighter.\",\n    \"Ship mass is not mine to set, and this is the one place the catalog constrains it. GDD 2.3.5 says a full hold at starting storage roughly doubles the rocket's mass; that holds here if the staged ship is around 1 t and the player is filling suborbital slots with mediums. If the crew prices the ship far below that, every mass in this catalog should be scaled by the same factor rather than re-authored piecewise — and the same instruction applies if the jetpack case above needs another pass.\",\n    \"The fragile gradient is spawn-weighted, not counted: suborbital 9/87 = 0.103, low 12/67 = 0.179, high 14/56 = 0.250. By piece count the three bands would read 2/8, 3/8 and 4/8 (0.25/0.375/0.50), which is why the fragile pieces carry the lowest weights in every band — a fragile piece has to be rare in encounter terms, not just rare in the type list.\",\n    \"No piece is strictly best, because mass and slot cost are deliberately decoupled. The insulation blanket wad is nearly free to tow and still costs a whole crushed slot; the platinum thruster cluster is one slot holding 540 kg. So the greedy choice at the tether is not the greedy choice at the hold, and the player has to decide which resource is scarce on this particular run.\",\n    \"Every size class and the fragile flag are all reachable inside the shipping slice. Suborbital and low hold five and four small pieces, two and three mediums, and two and three fragiles respectively, so nothing about the vocabulary waits on the deferred high band. The low band now meets the fragile flag at both size classes, which is what makes the detour a judgement call rather than a single all-or-nothing question.\",\n    \"Oversized is one piece per band and nothing more: derelict upper stage, tumbling comsat core, mirrored survey array. All three are crane-cable only and expected to be unreachable this semester. The high band's is fragile on purpose, so the fragile-and-oversized class the win condition belongs to exists in the catalog before the satellite does.\",\n    \"Mr. Armstrong's satellite is deliberately not in this catalog. The Researcher puts it above the high band at ~360 km, and the charter asks for exactly three bands; it is a named capstone object, not a spawn-table entry, and pricing it as ordinary loot would be wrong.\"\n  ]\n}","ttft_ms":72439,"ttft_stream_ms":1692,"time_to_request_ms":214,"type":"result","duration_ms":141666,"uuid":"9d847eca-df97-45cf-91ad-cc05e593b928"}
